# Mosquitto ACL: least privilege for z2m-guard
#
# Drop-in for /mosquitto/config/acl and add to mosquitto.conf:
#     acl_file /mosquitto/config/acl
#
# Two facts that make this safe to roll out:
#  1. With acl_file set, an authenticated user has NO rights unless listed here.
#  2. MQTT does not report ACL denials to the publisher at QoS 0/1 — a denied
#     publish is silently dropped and still gets its PUBACK. The only proof is a
#     second client listening on the topic and receiving nothing.

# The existing service user keeps its broad access: Home Assistant subscribes to
# homeassistant/#, Zigbee2MQTT publishes every device topic, Node-RED bridges.
user hass
topic readwrite #

# z2m-guard gets exactly what it uses, nothing else.
user z2mguard
# reads the shared availability topic of all Zigbee entities
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/state
# its own verdict topics (state, suppress, availability, last_restart)
topic readwrite z2m_guard/#
# its own Home Assistant discovery configs — and only those two domains
topic write homeassistant/binary_sensor/z2m_guard/#
topic write homeassistant/sensor/z2m_guard/#

# Not granted, on purpose: any device topic (zigbee2mqtt/<device>), bridge
# commands (zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/#), foreign discovery topics, $SYS.